  "liveTurns": 0,
  "harness": "scripts/cdp-m0-07-diagnostics.mjs (reject, stderr, verify; plan and verdict need no app)",
  "build": "pre-fix = 6e908f9; fixed = 6e908f9 + this commit's renderer changes. The worktree also held another proof's uncommitted approval changes (main.rs, ApprovalPanel.tsx, useMuseSessions.ts, approvalResolution.ts), outside these paths.",
  "summary": {
    "forgedRejection": "fixed: pass; pre-fix: fail (unsentRowBoundedMasked, composerLineBoundedMasked, noSecretInDom)",
    "stderrFlood": "fixed: pass; pre-fix: fail (noticeAndPillBoundedMasked, recoveryPanelBoundedMasked)",
    "exportAndStorage": "fixed: pass; pre-fix: fail (webStorageWhileUnsent, nativeOutboxMirrorWhileUnsent)"
  },
  "method": {
    "forgedRejection": "Real engine, no turn. The conversation's first send_input, its Retry and a composer follow-up are answered with a forged engine rejection. The page-side fetch layer (Tauri's IPC transport) re-points the request at a session id the bridge does not know, so send_input fails in session_client before any engine; the bridge's own error envelope (status 200, Tauri-Response: error, application/json) is kept and only its body is replaced. The body is exactly what msp.rs returns for an MSP error frame on turn/start: RpcError Display 'MSP error -32000: <message> [commandRejected] (m0_07_forged) [retryable=false]', which send_input passes unchanged. Message A: 5,316 chars, emoji/CJK/combining marks, an emoji pair across unit 500 of the renderer's bound, token=SYNTH-SECRET-<hex> before and after it. Message B: 5,315 chars, the secret value itself across unit 500 before redaction.",
    "stderrFlood": "debug\\muse.exe (the sidecar the dev build spawns first) backed up, replaced by a 20-line Rust fake, restored in a finally block and its SHA-256 compared with src-tauri/binaries (equal after both runs). The fake writes 237,616 bytes of stderr (420 lines, one of 105,448 bytes, 423 secrets), one non-JSON stdout line, reads the initialize request and exits: the real pump, push_stderr, the 20-line tail and the handshake error carry it. The boot resume (silent) and an explicit Reconnect of the test conversation fail through that path. Emoji were placed across UTF-8 byte 1000 of a line and byte 8000 of the tail (bridge cuts), unit 216 of the notice, unit 499 of the exported error and unit 3999 of the recovery panel.",
    "exportAndStorage": "Settings > Export diagnostics after each scenario, saved by WebView2 through CDP Browser.setDownloadBehavior and compared with the Blob the page built; collect_diagnostics read directly. localStorage and sessionStorage scanned live; Roaming and Local app data (caches skipped) byte-scanned as UTF-8 and UTF-16LE for every sentinel the harness generated."
  },
  "defects": [
    {
      "surface": "Unsent-message row, composer refusal line, stored outbox (localStorage muse-desktop.outbox.v1.<sid> and the native outbox/outbox.json mirror)",
      "preFix": "the engine's raw rejection: 5,335 units on screen with the synthetic secret visible; the same text written to both stores while the message stayed unsent",
      "fix": "src/lib/outbox.ts: sendFailed and markFailed pass the reason through redactDiagnostic (500 units, code-point safe, masked)",
      "test": "test/outbox.test.ts",
      "fixedBuild": "rows and composer line 500-501 units, token=[redacted], no secret in the DOM or in either store"
    },
    {
      "surface": "Connection pill title and notice (M0-08)",
      "preFix": "plain slice(0, 217): an emoji across unit 216 left a lone high surrogate (rendered as U+FFFD); no renderer masking",
      "fix": "src/lib/errorCopy.ts connectionNoticeText (masked, safeSlice), used by recordConnectionFailure in useMuseSessions.ts",
      "test": "test/errorCopy.test.ts",
      "fixedBuild": "217 units, emoji kept whole, no lone surrogate"
    },
    {
      "surface": "Recovery panel (SidecarErrorPanel, sanitizeStartupText 4,000)",
      "preFix": "plain slice(0, 4000): lone high surrogate at unit 3999",
      "fix": "src/lib/startupProbe.ts: safeSlice",
      "test": "test/startupProbe.test.ts",
      "fixedBuild": "3,999 units, no lone surrogate"
    }
  ],
  "observations": [
    "No panic: the bridge's byte cuts landed mid-emoji (line byte 1000, tail byte 8000) and it backed off to a character boundary; the 8,066-byte handshake error equals the harness model exactly, with 20 [redacted] marks and no U+FFFD.",
    "Already safe before the fix: the error banner (userFacingError, 500 units), the exported lastError (500 units) and collect_diagnostics (counters and engine versions only).",
    "msp.rs passes an engine RPC error message unbounded and unmasked (the 5,316-char message crosses as is); every renderer surface now bounds and masks it except the recovery panel, which only bounds (reachable only by an engine message inside a start failure; stderr is masked by the bridge).",
    "Not driven natively: the turn/completed failure card (parseTurnCompletion, unit-tested with the same straddles) and the skill lane detail, which still receives the raw send failure.",
    "The Settings export downloads at once; the plan's preview before export does not exist.",
    "Test data: one conversation per reject run (three today) in <proof>/m0-07-project, left in place with their unsent probes discarded. The project list is full (5/5), so the default folder was pointed at that folder for the start and restored after each run."
  ],
